WEBVTT

00:00.850 --> 00:04.340
<i>In a certain town, there lived a little girl.</i>

00:04.780 --> 00:08.650
<i>One day, the girl went to 
the forest to look for herbs</i>

00:08.650 --> 00:11.110
<i>for her sick and bedridden mother.</i>

00:11.380 --> 00:14.820
<i>However, since the forest 
was full of scary monsters,</i>

00:15.070 --> 00:18.280
<i>the girl was attacked by them.</i>

00:18.280 --> 00:20.680
<i>I'm sorry, Mom!</i>

00:20.680 --> 00:24.250
<i>I'm sorry I couldn't find 
the medicinal herbs for you!</i>

00:25.540 --> 00:31.830
<i>Right then, a bear suddenly 
appeared and saved the girl.</i>

00:32.560 --> 00:35.580
<i>Bear, are you going to eat me?</i>

00:36.220 --> 00:37.850
<i>I'm not.</i>

00:37.850 --> 00:42.150
<i>The girl explained to the bear 
why she came to the forest.</i>

00:42.150 --> 00:43.310
<i>Then...</i>

00:43.750 --> 00:50.230
<i>The bear carried the girl on her back and 
took her to a place with lots of herbs.</i>

00:50.760 --> 00:54.950
<i>Now the girl would be able to 
make medicine for her mother.</i>

00:54.950 --> 00:59.290
<i>Then, the bear took her back to town.</i>

01:00.310 --> 01:03.370
<i>Thank you, Bear. Thank you.</i>

01:03.870 --> 01:08.580
<i>The girl smiled and waved at the bear 
until it returned to the forest.</i>

01:09.060 --> 01:11.910
<i>She kept waving and waving...</i>

01:15.180 --> 01:19.220
So, that was the first picture book I made.

01:20.820 --> 01:21.430
Hm?

01:21.430 --> 01:22.450
Don't you remember?

01:22.450 --> 01:26.520
Kumayuru and Kumakyu, didn't we go 
visit Princess Flora in the royal capital

01:26.520 --> 01:28.620
after getting her letter?

01:28.620 --> 01:33.730
Princess Flora said she wanted to read the 
next part of the picture book I gave her,

01:33.730 --> 01:35.690
so I'm trying to think of what to draw.

01:37.310 --> 01:38.160
Oh, yeah.

01:38.160 --> 01:42.240
I modeled the girl after Fina, 
but Fina is pretty shy, right?

01:42.240 --> 01:46.080
So you two have to keep 
this whole thing a secret.

01:44.410 --> 01:46.080
Yuna Sis!

01:46.080 --> 01:48.790
I'm done harvesting the monsters for today.

01:48.790 --> 01:51.220
G-Good job, Fina!

01:51.750 --> 01:53.340
What's wrong?

01:53.340 --> 01:55.510
N-Nothing!

02:01.100 --> 02:05.350
<b>Bear Comes Home</b>

02:01.100 --> 02:05.350
<b>Bear Comes Home</b>

02:06.330 --> 02:08.190
Oh! Miss Bear!

02:08.190 --> 02:10.650
Yay! It's Bear Sis!

02:11.110 --> 02:13.060
Hey! Still a bear, like usual!

02:13.480 --> 02:16.820
Want a roasted skewer later, Miss Bear?

02:18.130 --> 02:19.530
What's up, Fina?

02:19.530 --> 02:23.040
I was just thinking about 
how popular you are, Yuna Sis.

02:25.170 --> 02:28.260
It's just that this bear 
costume really stands out.

02:30.660 --> 02:33.380
Here are your three puddings!

02:33.380 --> 02:35.590
Here's your pizza set!

02:35.590 --> 02:37.420
Thank you for the meal!

02:41.040 --> 02:42.800
So good!

02:42.800 --> 02:48.640
These new honey-soaked bear pancakes
 are really good, Yuna Sis!

02:48.640 --> 02:49.270
Yeah.

02:49.270 --> 02:54.730
Sweet honey generously drizzled 
over fluffy pancakes is the best!

02:54.730 --> 02:57.150
I don't really care for 
the bear shape though.

02:57.150 --> 02:59.900
What? But the bears are so cute!

03:00.500 --> 03:02.660
Don't you think so, too, Sis?!

03:02.660 --> 03:03.720
Y-Yeah.

03:03.720 --> 03:06.370
Why are you here, Shuri?

03:06.370 --> 03:08.200
I'm here with Mom!

03:08.500 --> 03:09.610
Mom?

03:09.610 --> 03:14.170
The guild master of the merchant 
guild, Miss Milaine, too?

03:14.170 --> 03:19.090
We're here to eat delicious food... 
is what I wish we could say...

03:19.090 --> 03:21.260
There's a little bit of a problem.

03:22.580 --> 03:23.840
Did something happen?

03:23.840 --> 03:29.680
Well, it looks like we won't be 
able to serve items that use honey soon.

03:29.680 --> 03:31.830
Including those pancakes, of course.

03:31.830 --> 03:32.900
Huh?!

03:34.980 --> 03:36.480
So yummy!

03:36.480 --> 03:40.300
Bad Shuri. Don't eat it so messily.

03:40.910 --> 03:44.390
The price of honey has shot up recently.

03:44.390 --> 03:45.910
Why's that?

03:46.290 --> 03:50.690
A problem occurred at the source of 
our supply, and all trade of it has stopped.

03:50.690 --> 03:55.750
So we have to stop selling items that use
 honey or drastically increase their price.

03:55.750 --> 03:58.960
Stop selling or raise the price...

03:58.960 --> 04:03.940
Items that use honey are really popular, 
so we don't want to take them off the menu.

04:03.940 --> 04:05.550
Most importantly...

04:08.640 --> 04:10.270
Sweet and fluffy!

04:10.270 --> 04:12.700
...the children love them.

04:13.730 --> 04:17.630
It'd be terrible if the children 
couldn't eat honey anymore.

04:17.630 --> 04:18.940
Um!

04:18.940 --> 04:21.650
What's the problem that caused all of this?

04:21.880 --> 04:23.370
Monsters.

04:23.370 --> 04:28.120
They've nested near the bee tree, so the
 workers can't collect the honey anymore.

04:28.120 --> 04:30.820
Monsters nested near the beehives?

04:30.820 --> 04:34.040
No, the bee tree.

04:34.040 --> 04:37.250
Tree? I didn't mishear you?

04:37.250 --> 04:39.920
Oh, you didn't know?

04:39.920 --> 04:46.220
Hundreds of thousands of bees gather 
together to make a single giant bee tree.

04:46.220 --> 04:48.000
Hundreds of thousands?

04:50.140 --> 04:51.930
That sounds gross...

04:51.930 --> 04:56.170
Even without monsters, wouldn't that be 
a problem for people collecting honey?

04:56.170 --> 04:58.610
They're a very docile species.

04:59.650 --> 05:01.730
So what kind of monster 
is causing the problem?

05:01.730 --> 05:05.440
The bee tree's keeper said they were orcs.

05:05.440 --> 05:08.120
They posted a request at 
the adventurer's guild,

05:08.120 --> 05:10.490
but who knows when someone 
will take care of it?

05:10.490 --> 05:12.450
Orcs, huh? Okay!

05:12.450 --> 05:13.600
Yuna?

05:13.600 --> 05:15.750
I'll go ask about it at the adventurer's guild.

05:17.250 --> 05:19.590
I thought you'd say that, Yuna!

05:20.560 --> 05:22.300
Did you tell me about it on purpose?

05:22.300 --> 05:24.260
Huh? What are you talking about?!

05:25.630 --> 05:28.470
I'm going out for a bit, Fina.

05:28.470 --> 05:31.010
Okay. Be careful.

05:32.950 --> 05:35.520
Hunting the monsters near the bee tree?

05:35.520 --> 05:38.980
No one has taken that quest yet.

05:38.980 --> 05:41.620
Even though there are so many adventurers?

05:41.620 --> 05:42.440
About that...

05:42.440 --> 05:45.770
After some scouting, we found out 
that it was a horde of orcs

05:45.770 --> 05:47.780
instead of individuals around the bee tree.

05:47.780 --> 05:50.350
A horde of them?

05:51.000 --> 05:51.960
Okay.

05:54.480 --> 05:55.940
Welp, Kumayuru...

05:56.900 --> 05:59.370
Why don't you run and take me 
to this bee tree?

06:01.630 --> 06:03.210
Be careful, young lady!

06:03.210 --> 06:04.230
I will.

06:11.110 --> 06:12.250
That's right.

06:12.250 --> 06:16.410
Miss Helen said that the bee tree 
would be near the center of this forest.

06:16.410 --> 06:19.270
She said there's no way we'd miss it...

06:32.290 --> 06:34.530
This is the bee tree?

06:37.960 --> 06:41.880
I know it's kinda late, but this really 
makes me feel like I'm in another world.

06:43.320 --> 06:44.210
But...

06:45.330 --> 06:49.430
No matter what world I'm in, there's always 
something that likes to destroy the scenery.

06:49.850 --> 06:52.710
And they're hogging all the honey, too.

06:52.710 --> 06:53.870
Unforgivable!

06:55.020 --> 06:56.180
What's wrong?

06:58.550 --> 06:59.270
Huh?!

06:59.270 --> 07:01.580
Moving rocks?!

07:01.580 --> 07:04.430
Wait, are those bears?!

07:04.430 --> 07:07.530
Bears from this world? Real ones?!

07:07.530 --> 07:10.430
No, Kumayuru and Kumakyu are real, too!

07:10.430 --> 07:12.410
Bears?! Real bears?!

07:13.530 --> 07:15.460
They both look pretty beat-up?

07:17.290 --> 07:21.170
Are they fighting for territory
 near the bee tree?

07:24.330 --> 07:27.750
Well, I'd like to help the bears, too.

07:27.750 --> 07:31.680
But depending on the situation, 
we might have to fight the bears, too.

07:33.140 --> 07:37.600
Well, yeah. The quest 
didn't include the bears.

07:43.160 --> 07:44.150
A baby bear?!

07:49.990 --> 07:50.810
Wha?!

08:11.300 --> 08:15.080
<i>The bears might attack humans, too.</i>

08:15.080 --> 08:18.760
<i>Saving them here might not 
be the right thing to do.</i>

08:20.600 --> 08:22.560
<i>Even so, I...</i>

08:25.920 --> 08:30.610
I can't stand anyone that hurts kids!

08:33.450 --> 08:35.760
I'll take you all down!

08:36.650 --> 08:39.020
Bear Cutter!

08:42.680 --> 08:45.270
Bear Punch!

08:48.070 --> 08:50.130
Now, what should I do?

08:50.130 --> 08:53.730
My quest is just to hunt down the orcs.

08:53.730 --> 08:58.480
But at this rate, this family of bears 
will just take their place.

08:58.480 --> 09:01.340
You want me to heal their wounds?

09:02.510 --> 09:04.940
Well, I can't say no to you guys.

09:07.370 --> 09:08.240
Heal.

09:12.840 --> 09:16.250
I healed your wounds, but you'll
 need to take it easy for a while.

09:18.780 --> 09:20.650
Are you thanking me?

09:20.650 --> 09:22.630
It's fine. Don't worry about it.

09:22.630 --> 09:25.110
I'm a bear, too.

09:25.110 --> 09:26.960
But what should I do about this?

09:27.490 --> 09:28.910
Hey, guys.

09:29.430 --> 09:32.800
Can you stay away from the humans 
that come to gather honey here?

09:33.420 --> 09:35.790
Not that you understand what I'm saying.

09:37.940 --> 09:38.730
Huh?

09:39.880 --> 09:42.310
Huh? Take the honey?

09:42.310 --> 09:44.660
No, I'm not talking about me!

09:46.200 --> 09:51.830
So, in the end, the bears gave me honey 
for taking care of the monsters.

09:51.830 --> 09:53.930
I see. Bears...

09:53.930 --> 09:56.110
I don't really want to hunt the bears.

09:56.110 --> 09:58.200
It can't be helped.

09:58.200 --> 10:02.200
Asking you to hunt down bears is 
like asking you to destroy yourself.

10:02.610 --> 10:05.050
<i>Huh? Did I look that serious?!</i>

10:05.050 --> 10:06.910
You hunted the bears?!

10:07.290 --> 10:08.330
Mister Rem...

10:08.330 --> 10:12.960
How terrible. They just had cubs!

10:12.960 --> 10:15.020
Miss Helen, who is this?

10:15.020 --> 10:17.050
Oh, yes. Mister Rem here is the 
one who posted the quest.

10:17.050 --> 10:19.220
He's the keeper of the bee tree.

10:19.220 --> 10:22.870
I came to see if anyone 
took care of my request,

10:22.870 --> 10:24.740
I can't believe the bears got hurt, too.

10:24.740 --> 10:28.230
Excuse me... I think you misunderstood.

10:29.140 --> 10:32.110
I'm sorry, I couldn't help 
overhearing about the bears...

10:32.110 --> 10:34.520
You knew that bears were living there?

10:34.520 --> 10:39.040
Yes. They've saved us 
from monsters many times.

10:39.610 --> 10:43.840
In exchange for their protection 
while we tend to the flowers,

10:43.840 --> 10:47.360
we turn a blind eye when 
they take some honey.

10:47.360 --> 10:49.250
It's a symbiotic relationship.

10:49.250 --> 10:51.810
Please inform us about things 
like that from the beginning!

10:51.810 --> 10:55.460
The bears might have been 
hunted down along with the orcs!

10:55.460 --> 10:58.120
I'm sorry.

10:58.120 --> 11:01.790
I was worried that the bears 
would be hunted down

11:01.790 --> 11:04.550
if our lord found out about them.

11:04.550 --> 11:06.920
Lord? You mean Cliff?

11:06.920 --> 11:09.220
Why would he do anything about the bee tree?

11:09.220 --> 11:13.490
You're the only one who can speak 
about our local lord so casually, Yuna.

11:13.490 --> 11:15.370
Bee trees are exceedingly rare,

11:15.370 --> 11:17.500
and the responsibility of the 
feudal lord who owns the land.

11:17.500 --> 11:20.410
Yes. I was just hired as a keeper.

11:20.410 --> 11:22.610
Our lord has the final say on everything.

11:23.410 --> 11:24.920
Oh, that's right.

11:24.920 --> 11:27.360
Cliff owes me a lot of favors,

11:27.360 --> 11:30.120
so bring my name up when 
you explain the situation.

11:32.180 --> 11:34.950
To even say Lord Cliff owes you favors...

11:34.950 --> 11:36.960
Miss Yuna, you're so...

11:36.960 --> 11:41.800
In exchange, please let those bears 
live peacefully at the bee tree.

11:42.970 --> 11:44.630
Yes, of course!

11:44.630 --> 11:47.160
Thank you so much, Miss Bear!

11:48.480 --> 11:52.350
I'm so glad that the price 
of honey has gone down again.

11:52.350 --> 11:57.520
We can keep the customers happy! 
You saved us again, Miss Yuna.

11:57.520 --> 12:02.020
I just wanted to keep eating delicious things.

12:02.020 --> 12:06.160
So, Ms. Morin, please continue 
making me delicious bread and food.

12:06.160 --> 12:08.410
Of course. Leave it to me.

12:08.410 --> 12:10.080
Enjoy!

12:10.080 --> 12:12.680
You're amazing, Yuna Sis.

12:12.680 --> 12:15.140
Not really.

12:15.620 --> 12:17.750
But it makes me happy that you think that way.

12:20.970 --> 12:22.760
Sorry to intrude during closing hours.

12:22.760 --> 12:25.160
I was hoping that Yuna was here...

12:25.160 --> 12:26.640
I found you, Miss Yuna!

12:26.640 --> 12:28.690
Huh?! N-Noir?!

12:27.100 --> 12:28.690
L-Lady Noir?

12:28.690 --> 12:30.950
You're so fluffy, Miss Yuna!

12:30.950 --> 12:32.810
Nice to see you, Fina!

12:32.810 --> 12:36.150
Goodness! Please come 
visit my home occasionally!

12:36.150 --> 12:37.770
Th-That's a bit...

12:38.440 --> 12:43.550
Could this be the new menu item, 
honey-soaked bear pancakes?!

12:43.550 --> 12:46.740
This loveliness! Truly bear-like!

12:46.740 --> 12:50.950
I-If you'd like some, I can have 
Ms. Morin make you some.

12:50.950 --> 12:52.300
Really?!

12:53.660 --> 12:56.780
I get to eat pancakes with Miss Yuna!

12:56.780 --> 12:58.040
Noir.

12:58.040 --> 13:02.630
Didn't you promise me that you wouldn't 
bother Yuna and I if you came along?

13:02.630 --> 13:05.740
That's right. Then...

13:06.330 --> 13:10.540
Fina, let's not bother their 
conversation and go over there.

13:09.540 --> 13:11.180
Huh? L-Lady Noir?!

13:11.180 --> 13:14.640
I had something to discuss with you 
regarding the fan club, Fina.

13:15.540 --> 13:17.350
Um, o-okay.

13:18.320 --> 13:20.190
Our plans are coming along!

13:20.190 --> 13:21.940
Sorry for the noise, Yuna.

13:21.940 --> 13:23.740
Well, I don't mind Noir.

13:23.740 --> 13:26.830
So, what did you want to talk to me about?

13:29.590 --> 13:33.730
<i>Dear Sister Noir and Fina, 
I hope you both are doing well.</i>

13:33.730 --> 13:39.110
<i>I enjoyed the time I spent with the two 
of you in the royal capital very much.</i>

13:39.110 --> 13:42.990
<i>This time, I would like to 
invite you to visit my home.</i>

13:42.990 --> 13:48.150
<i>I look forward to seeing the two of you 
and Sister Yuna once again.</i>

13:48.150 --> 13:50.010
Lady Misa seems to be doing well.

13:50.010 --> 13:54.440
Yes. She is looking forward to 
our fan club meeting.

13:54.440 --> 13:59.350
So, please report about the bee tree, 
fan club vice president!

13:59.350 --> 14:03.570
Um, I didn't witness it in person...

14:03.570 --> 14:07.780
But it all started with 
the honey-soaked bear pancakes.

14:08.210 --> 14:12.830
Ellalaura sent a letter from 
the royal capital addressed to you.

14:13.140 --> 14:16.730
It seems like Princess Flora 
wants to see your bears again.

14:16.730 --> 14:18.640
Princess Flora?

14:20.880 --> 14:25.300
Also, it seems like Ellalaura has 
something to discuss with you herself.

14:25.650 --> 14:27.870
Miss Ellalaura wants to see me?

14:29.010 --> 14:35.450
<i>She's a lot more elusive to me than Cliff...</i>

14:35.450 --> 14:38.300
<i>She's not a bad person though.</i>

14:38.300 --> 14:41.520
Sorry for asking this, but could 
you visit the royal capital?

14:41.520 --> 14:45.930
<i>Well, I </i>did<i> finish the next picture book.</i>

14:45.930 --> 14:49.480
Sure. I want to treat them to pancakes, too.

14:50.150 --> 14:51.070
Thanks.

14:51.070 --> 14:53.780
Oh, I heard from Mister Rem.

14:54.160 --> 14:57.250
You allowed the bears to 
live near the bee tree, right?

14:57.570 --> 14:58.640
Thank you.

14:58.640 --> 15:03.770
Oh, that was nothing compared 
to the stress your tunnel caused me.

15:03.770 --> 15:06.020
Uh, sorry for causing you trouble.

15:06.020 --> 15:07.090
I was kidding.

15:07.090 --> 15:10.710
Well, the tunnel will be officially 
open to the public soon.

15:10.710 --> 15:12.680
Things will become even busier.

15:13.050 --> 15:14.030
Really?

15:14.030 --> 15:19.080
That mean Miss Anz will be 
opening a restaurant here soon.

15:20.320 --> 15:21.640
I can't wait!

15:25.860 --> 15:27.190
Miss Bear!

15:27.190 --> 15:29.380
Hello, Princess Flora.

15:29.830 --> 15:30.650
Oh, my.

15:30.650 --> 15:33.870
You really love Yuna, Princess Flora.

15:33.870 --> 15:36.830
Oh, my! She really is a bear.

15:36.830 --> 15:38.950
Right? It's just as I said.

15:39.360 --> 15:42.420
Hey, why are the king and...

15:42.420 --> 15:44.110
It's mother!

15:44.110 --> 15:46.450
Nice to meet you. My name is Kitia.

15:46.450 --> 15:50.470
I've heard a lot about you 
from His Majesty and my child.

15:50.470 --> 15:52.050
Um, I'm Yuna.

15:52.050 --> 15:53.010
I'm Ellalaura!

15:53.010 --> 15:54.320
I know!

15:56.210 --> 16:00.410
Flora always tells me that 
Miss Bear is very cute.

16:01.160 --> 16:02.940
I see that it's true.

16:02.940 --> 16:04.150
Cute!

16:09.520 --> 16:11.320
Here you go, Princess Flora.

16:11.320 --> 16:13.860
Wow! Bears!

16:13.860 --> 16:18.500
This is our new menu item, 
honey-soaked bear pancakes.

16:18.950 --> 16:20.470
It's delicious.

16:20.470 --> 16:22.120
Thank you for the meal!

16:25.730 --> 16:27.040
Yummy!

16:27.040 --> 16:29.910
This is delicious, but is there no pudding?

16:29.910 --> 16:32.100
Don't be rude, Your Majesty.

16:32.100 --> 16:36.140
However, it's true I still can't forget 
the flavor of the pudding from the banquet.

16:36.140 --> 16:41.470
My chef could make it and I would be 
able to eat it every day if I had the recipe.

16:41.470 --> 16:43.310
So true...

16:43.720 --> 16:46.150
Pudding? I love it, too!

16:47.080 --> 16:50.730
I understand. I'll prepare the recipe for you.

16:51.200 --> 16:54.120
But please don't tell other people.

16:54.120 --> 16:55.220
Truly?

16:55.220 --> 16:56.500
I promise you.

16:56.500 --> 16:59.880
And, it's not good to eat too much of it. 
Make sure you don't eat more than one a day.

17:01.910 --> 17:05.870
Um, Princess Flora, 
I have another gift for you.

17:06.300 --> 17:07.650
Please take this.

17:07.650 --> 17:09.210
A bear picture book!

17:09.210 --> 17:12.450
Mother! It's a bear picture book!

17:12.450 --> 17:17.140
Is this the continuation of 
the picture book Flora loves to read?

17:17.140 --> 17:20.850
Princess Flora said she 
wanted to read more, so...

17:20.850 --> 17:24.320
Yuna, can I make copies 
of this picture book?

17:24.320 --> 17:24.930
Huh?

17:24.930 --> 17:29.710
Wouldn't Princess Flora be sad 
if this book accidentally got destroyed?

17:29.710 --> 17:32.970
If we had copies, she could 
always carry it around with her.

17:32.970 --> 17:35.230
Well, yeah, that's true.

17:35.230 --> 17:38.990
If I make copies, can I pass it out 
to people who want it?

17:38.990 --> 17:40.120
Yeah.

17:40.120 --> 17:41.450
Wait, what?!

17:41.450 --> 17:44.310
Actually, a lot of officials and servants

17:44.310 --> 17:47.800
want to read your picture 
books to their children.

17:47.800 --> 17:48.420
Huh?

17:48.420 --> 17:52.170
Princess Flora goes around reading 
her picture book everywhere she goes.

17:52.170 --> 17:55.840
Right now, there are a lot of fans 
of your picture book within the castle.

17:55.840 --> 17:57.860
It's already known to others?!

17:57.860 --> 18:00.350
But that's pretty embarrassing...

18:00.350 --> 18:01.430
Please!

18:01.430 --> 18:03.370
I'd like to ask as well.

18:03.370 --> 18:05.140
I, as well.

18:05.460 --> 18:07.260
I dunno...

18:12.110 --> 18:15.340
<i>She's so absorbed in my picture book.</i>

18:16.990 --> 18:21.780
All right. Please only pass
it around within the castle.

18:21.780 --> 18:23.520
I appreciate it.

18:23.520 --> 18:26.170
Ellalaura, please take care of it.

18:26.170 --> 18:27.420
Yes, Your Majesty.

18:27.420 --> 18:30.960
I'll send you a bunch of copies 
once I'm done, Yuna.

18:30.960 --> 18:33.050
Yeah. Thanks.

18:34.920 --> 18:37.360
Thank you for the pudding recipe.

18:37.360 --> 18:39.470
Well, I promised.

18:39.470 --> 18:43.480
I didn't think that the head chef 
would be that thankful.

18:43.480 --> 18:46.640
It's the head chef's job to make 
food that the royal family enjoys.

18:46.640 --> 18:51.980
The head chef was really moved 
by the pudding during the banquet.

18:51.980 --> 18:53.610
That makes me happy, but...

18:53.610 --> 18:57.820
<i>I wasn't the creator of that recipe though.</i>

18:58.280 --> 18:58.900
Now, then.

18:58.900 --> 19:02.240
Now that all of that is finished, I have 
something personal to talk to you about.

19:02.240 --> 19:04.330
Oh, Cliff said something about that?

19:05.510 --> 19:08.910
<i>I wonder why her smile 
makes me a little uneasy?</i>

19:08.910 --> 19:11.370
<i>Is this the instinct of a bear?</i>

19:11.650 --> 19:14.330
I'd like to request the adventurer Yuna

19:14.330 --> 19:16.890
guard the students 
of the royal capital academy.

19:16.890 --> 19:18.460
Guard the students?

19:18.460 --> 19:21.690
The top students of the academy are 
going outside of the royal capital

19:21.690 --> 19:24.720
for some hands-on training.

19:25.220 --> 19:27.930
They'll be traveling to 
a nearby village and back.

19:28.340 --> 19:31.230
During their trip, they'll learn
 the hardship of travel,

19:31.230 --> 19:36.190
the difficulties of camping, and how to 
trust their fellow students and guardians.

19:38.080 --> 19:42.770
I understand the reason, but isn't it 
the academy's job to hire guardians?

19:42.770 --> 19:44.240
Why are you asking me?

19:44.240 --> 19:46.700
I run various errands for the academy.

19:46.700 --> 19:49.660
<i>Didn't you say you ran various 
errands for the castle before?!</i>

19:49.660 --> 19:52.990
Well, aren't the students 
of the academy noble children?

19:52.990 --> 19:56.480
We can't find any good 
adventurers to guard the children

19:56.480 --> 19:59.760
since a lot of them think 
they're rude and naïve.

19:59.760 --> 20:05.080
You're close to their age 
and plenty strong for the job.

20:04.120 --> 20:06.350
No, no. I can't do it, either.

20:06.350 --> 20:08.860
I don't like being around kids my age,

20:08.860 --> 20:11.020
and noble children are 
definitely a lot of trouble.

20:11.020 --> 20:15.100
<i>It'll be too difficult for a shut-in like me, 
who stopped going to school.</i>

20:15.530 --> 20:16.660
It'll be fine.

20:16.660 --> 20:20.690
Even if you punish them a bit, 
I'll use my power to cover it up.

20:20.690 --> 20:22.900
Did you just say you'd abuse your power?!

20:23.900 --> 20:26.620
Um, I'm actually a pretty busy girl.

20:26.620 --> 20:27.620
Really?

20:27.620 --> 20:28.700
With the restaurant...

20:28.700 --> 20:30.410
<i>In order to eat delicious things,</i>

20:30.410 --> 20:32.230
I need to check in regularly.

20:32.230 --> 20:33.120
At the orphanage...

20:33.120 --> 20:34.960
<i>To play with the kids,</i>

20:34.960 --> 20:37.420
I'm busy with regular inspections.

20:37.420 --> 20:41.170
Don't you have other people taking 
care of the restaurant, Bear Haven,

20:41.170 --> 20:42.990
and selling eggs through the orphanage?

20:42.990 --> 20:47.640
I'm sure their names were Ms. Morin, 
Miss Karin, and Miss Tiermina?

20:47.640 --> 20:50.720
<i>Hey, otherworld! Is there no privacy here?!</i>

20:50.720 --> 20:54.350
Don't worry. I'll make sure to assign you 
to the same group as my daughter.

20:54.350 --> 20:57.420
By daughter, you mean Shia?

20:57.420 --> 20:58.020
Yes.

20:58.020 --> 21:01.110
When I told her that you 
might become a guardian...

21:01.110 --> 21:05.550
I want to show Miss Yuna 
that I've gotten stronger!

21:07.470 --> 21:10.200
She started throwing herself into 
her training even harder than before.

21:11.530 --> 21:16.910
It'd be nice to see Shia again, and it'll
 be a little easier if she's there...

21:16.910 --> 21:19.670
Of course, we'll pay you, too.

21:19.670 --> 21:23.190
And how about I owe you one?

21:23.190 --> 21:25.130
My favors are much more 
valuable than Cliff's.

21:27.850 --> 21:28.970
All right.

21:28.970 --> 21:30.980
But only this one time.

21:30.980 --> 21:33.180
Thank you. I'll owe you one.

21:38.900 --> 21:39.980
I'm exhausted.

21:40.720 --> 21:42.180
Yuna Sis!

21:42.180 --> 21:42.940
Fina?

21:42.940 --> 21:46.490
You could have gone home after 
you finished today's harvest.

21:47.030 --> 21:51.120
But I still wanted to tell you 
after I finished my work, Yuna Sis.

21:51.120 --> 21:55.750
I'm glad I didn't stay overnight at the royal 
capital and used the Bear Transfer Gate.

21:55.750 --> 21:58.620
Oh! Shoot. I forgot something important.

21:59.670 --> 22:02.040
Welcome home, Yuna Sis!

22:02.550 --> 22:04.490
I'm home, Fina.

23:35.430 --> 23:40.020
<b>Bear, Watching Over Students</b>

23:35.470 --> 23:40.020
<b>Next Episode</b>

23:35.860 --> 23:37.580
Bear.
